WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.871
-With President Trump down by a
wide margin in the latest polls,

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:07.640
his campaign has landed
on a closing argument --

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.310
Spread coronavirus
to as many people as possible

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.178
and threaten to leave
the country if he loses.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:14.347
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:18.417 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:20.987
As of Saturday,
more than 26 million people

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.022
had already voted
in the presidential election,

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:26.593
breaking records everywhere from
Alabama to Georgia to Texas.

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:28.894
People lined up for hours
across the country,

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:31.364
including at some iconic sites
that have been converted

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:34.300
into polling places
like Fenway Park.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.570
-The enthusiasm was high among
voters casting their ballots

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.039
at Fenway Park.
-I wanted to vote at Fenway

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:42.642
because we have all been cooped
up inside for a little bit

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:44.411
and I got my Dunkies

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.846
and I'm ready to vote
for Joe Biden,

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.281
but I wish I was voting
for Bernie Sanders.

00:00:49.281 --> 00:00:50.750
But it's a team sport.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.018
-Fantastic.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.586
Even after the pandemic is over,

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.788
I hope Boston holds every
election at Fenway.

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:58.090
I'd love to see the exit polling
afterward.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.626
"Well, Wolf, I'm a little
shocked by these numbers,

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:03.930
but apparently 58% voted for
"Ya motha."

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.632
Usually the only election
at Fenway

00:01:06.632 --> 00:01:09.702 line:0%
are landslides in favor
of Jeter Sucks.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.437
And if you're wondering
what that one dot is...

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.406
[ Boston accent ] So, my uncle,
who is a big wig at Fleet

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.008
got me the bank's tickets
on Saturday,

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.542
so I invite Marty Snakes,
and he's all,

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:18.077
"Can I bring my friend?"
And I say, "Sure."

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.246
'Cause I owe him from that time
his cousin, who's a statie,

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:21.614
helped me out with that DUI.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.716
But Marty doesn't mention
his friend's a Yankee fan.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:26.252
Kid shows up with the hat and
everything, and on top of that,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.320
when Marty asks if we want
beers, the guy says,

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:30.022
"I'll take a IPA," and I'm like,
"IPA?

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:33.193
How about a Bud Light
and you shut the [bleep] up?"

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:35.595
That was like a little play.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.463
So, tens of millions of people
across the country

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:39.999
have already lined up to vote
or mailed in their ballot.

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:42.868
Now, we don't know what that
tells us about the outcome

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:44.704
except that it can't be great
news for Trump

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:47.406
since he is currently trailing
in national polls

00:01:47.406 --> 00:01:49.608
around 10 points, and he's
running out of time

00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:52.612
to make up the gap, which might
explain why he has been making

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:54.681
